{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1251822-scent-of-the-divine","id":1251822,"title":"Scent of the Divine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-05T20:23:09-07:00","id":1251822,"title":"Scent of the Divine","content":"I had a rather specific idea that didn\u2019t seem to justify a whole thread, so I thought I\u2019d use it as a jumping off point for a broader discussion.<br /> <br /> Do you think the Theoi Scent of the Divine description works well enough for their Roman Mantles, Scions, and distinctly Roman gods, Monsters, and spirits. I\u2019m the first to argue the Romans cribbed the bulk of their myths from the Greek and created a mythic narrative for themselves to make them the direct continuation of an Olympian worshipping civilization - so in Scion, yes Jupiter needs to be a Mantle of Zeus rather than the supreme god of a separate Pantheon - BUT, there are still enough differences that \u201colives in hot air and the murmurs of a crowd\u201d don\u2019t seem to fit great.<br /> <br /> If I was making a new Roman Pantheon without the Greek, I\u2019d make them smell like the Colosseum: boiling wine and saffron covering up blood and feces, with the distant sound of war trumpets.<br /> <br /> But that seems too divergent for a sub-Pantheon where most of its core gods are just Mantles of the same guys as the original Pantheon. Should I leave the olives the same, but replace the murmur of the crowd with the war trumpets?<br /> <br /> By all means, use this as a jumping off point to discuss other Pantheons and Scent of the Divine!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T21:07:53-07:00","id":1251829,"title":"","content":"I think the smell of olives should be in both, it serves as a common link between the two.<br /> <br /> I like to think that Scent The Dvine on sub pantheons is like sniffing a new offshoot from the same perfume brand, So in this case the Roman fragrance is a bolder, louder scent, you smell the same olives like usual but there's now the screaming war trumpets and vague undertone of blood and feces reflecting the now crowded, expansionist nature of the Roman Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T01:02:52-07:00","id":1251860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1251822-scent-of-the-divine?p=1251829#post1251829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the smell of olives should be in both, it serves as a common link between the two.<br /> <br /> I like to think that Scent The Dvine on sub pantheons is like sniffing a new offshoot from the same perfume brand, So in this case the Roman fragrance is a bolder, louder scent, you smell the same olives like usual but there's now the screaming war trumpets and vague undertone of blood and feces reflecting the now crowded, expansionist nature of the Roman Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works. Like I said, I wasn\u2019t sure if olives were resonant enough with Rome, and what the colosseum used to cover the stink was boiling wine with saffron, but I do like linking the scents together.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a separate note... the Netjer... sand has a smell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T18:55:32-07:00","id":1252074,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m leaning strongly toward making the Netjer smell \u201cperfumes and oils\u201d along with the sound of desert wind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T22:20:33-07:00","id":1252441,"title":"","content":"Some of the pantheons would logically be linked with unrecognizable scents. Example: a Southeast Asian pantheon might have a sacred incense that never got popular in the West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T11:13:09-07:00","id":1254800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1251822-scent-of-the-divine?p=1251860#post1251860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> On a separate note... the Netjer... sand has a smell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a sand specialist here, but... Desert (sand) has a different smell from beach (sand). This kind of sand often reminds me of a &quot;salty&quot; smell, but I think the desert one is a different approach.<br /> <br /> Indeed. &quot;perfumes and oils&quot; make a lot more sense for the Netjer imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T06:30:31-07:00","id":1254988,"title":"","content":"Olive oil was still pretty common in Rome, and indeed the entire Mediterranean. It might not have served the same vital social function for Rome as for Athens and Sparta, but it was omnipresent. Pliny the Elder is noted as having written that Italian olive oil was the finest in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T10:02:58-07:00","id":1255027,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s another issue: tobacco and rum make perfect sense for the Loa... but both are distinctly \u201cNew World\u201d scents, and less resonant with West Africa to work for the Orisha Mantles that haven\u2019t gone through the Middle Passage. Thoughts on better replacements there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}